#N canvas 20 20 1600 1080 12;
#X text 20 20 m_nano -- the nanoKONTROL mapping layer. Decodes CC into named parameters on disp \, and the transport buttons into mode \, start and stop. It knows NOTHING about what it controls: that is the point of the m_ layer and the one boundary that is genuinely expensive to retrofit., f 58;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel that the nano's OWN channel 1 lands on. REQUIRED -- without it nothing decodes. Transport is that channel plus one. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 250 THE CHANNEL BLOCK IS PD'S INPUT SLOT \, not the device's position in the system MIDI list. Pd gives input slot n the channels (n-1)*16+1 upward \, so the nano is 17 on the Organelle (slot 2 \, per .pdsettings) and 1 on the Mac when it is the only input opened. MEASURED both ways rather than inferred -- and that is exactly why this is an argument and not a constant., f 58;
#X obj 20 400 ctlin;
#X obj 340 470 s \$0-cc;
#X obj 660 470 - \$1;
#X obj 660 520 t f f;
#X obj 660 570 == 0;
#X obj 660 610 s \$0-ctl-on;
#X obj 820 570 == 1;
#X obj 820 610 s \$0-xport-on;
#X text 660 660 TWO FLAGS \, NOT ONE NUMBER \, because a channel from another device must set BOTH to zero. The nano shares the CC stream with the Launchpad and the 404 \, and quietly mistaking one for another is the failure this arithmetic exists to prevent., f 44;
#X obj 20 470 t f f;
#N canvas 30 30 1300 900 controls 0;
#X text 20 20 Sliders \, knobs and the eighteen buttons. The value arrives LAST \, so the name and the two kind flags are already decoded and waiting by the time it gets here., f 58;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 190 spigot;
#X obj 160 150 r \$0-ctl-on;
#X obj 20 250 t f f b;
#N canvas 30 30 1800 920 decode-name 0;
#X text 20 20 CC NUMBER IN \, A NAME AND TWO KIND FLAGS OUT -- all on \$0- sends \, because three results from one bang is what sends are for. Nothing in here touches the VALUE., f 58;
#X obj 20 150 inlet;
#X obj 20 200 f;
#X obj 160 160 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 20 250 t f f;
#X obj 20 310 div 10;
#X obj 20 360 t f f f;
#X obj 200 420 >= 2;
#X obj 200 460 s \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 380 420 < 2;
#X obj 380 460 s \$0-is-cont;
#X obj 560 310 mod 10;
#X obj 560 420 list prepend;
#X obj 560 480 route 0 1 2 3;
#X obj 560 550 makefilename slider-%d;
#X obj 560 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 800 550 makefilename knob-%d;
#X obj 800 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 1040 550 makefilename btn-t-%d;
#X obj 1040 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 1280 550 makefilename btn-b-%d;
#X obj 1280 600 s \$0-name;
#N canvas 40 40 900 620 unmapped 0;
#X text 20 20 A CC in this block that decodes to no known kind. It clears BOTH flags -- otherwise the arithmetic upstream would have left is-btn set \, and the next value would emit under the PREVIOUS control's name: plausible \, wrong \, and silent., f 52;
#X obj 20 120 inlet;
#X obj 20 170 t b b b;
#X msg 20 240 0;
#X obj 20 290 s \$0-is-cont;
#X msg 240 240 0;
#X obj 240 290 s \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 500 240 f;
#X obj 620 200 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 500 300 makefilename cc-%d-unmapped;
#X obj 500 350 list prepend warn m_nano;
#X obj 500 400 list trim;
#X obj 500 450 s err;
#X text 20 350 The clears come FIRST \, off the rightmost outlets \, and the error goes out last. Reversed \, a storm of unknown CCs could still leak one wrong parameter between the two., f 46;
#X text 20 500 THE list trim AGAIN. list prepend builds a list \; u_err's route matches a selector. Without it every m_nano warning would be dropped by the very bus that exists to stop things being silent., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 2 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 2 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 2 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 7 1;
#X connect 7 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X restore 1520 480 pd unmapped;
#X text 20 700 KIND AND WHICH \, PACKED \, THEN ROUTED. div 10 is the kind and mod 10 is which one -- the same idiom that already covers the Launchpad grid. Prepending the kind and routing on it gives each kind its OWN makefilename \, so there is no format to set and no ordering to get wrong., f 46;
#X text 620 700 route WITH FLOAT ARGUMENTS matches the first element of a LIST and strips it \, handing each makefilename just the number. This is the one place route's list behaviour is what you want rather than a trap to work around., f 46;
#X text 1180 700 FOUR NAMES \, FOUR PLACEHOLDERS: slider-1 \, knob-3 \, btn-t-5 \, btn-b-9. These four boxes are the seam where v0.3's real parameter names arrive \, and where the compose / perform mapping will eventually hang., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 1 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 6 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 4 0 11 0;
#X connect 6 2 12 1;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 13 1 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 13 2 18 0;
#X connect 18 0 19 0;
#X connect 13 3 20 0;
#X connect 20 0 21 0;
#X connect 13 4 22 0;
#X restore 700 310 pd decode-name;
#X obj 100 340 r \$0-is-cont;
#X obj 20 400 spigot;
#X obj 440 340 r \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 360 400 spigot;
#X obj 360 450 select 127;
#X msg 360 500 1;
#X obj 20 570 list prepend;
#X obj 560 530 r \$0-name;
#X obj 20 620 list trim;
#X obj 20 670 s disp;
#X text 820 400 The decode runs off the RIGHTMOST outlet \, so it has finished before either gate sees the value. That is why this needs no delay object anywhere., f 46;
#X text 20 730 ONE EMIT CHAIN \, FED BY TWO GATES. A fan-IN needs no trigger -- only a fan-out does -- so the continuous value and the button's 1 converge on the same list prepend \, whose cold inlet already holds the name., f 46;
#X text 420 730 BUTTONS EMIT ON PRESS ONLY. They are momentary \, 127 then 0 \, measured on this unit. Pd owns every toggle because the mk1 has no host-controllable LEDs \, so device-side state would silently desync., f 46;
#X text 820 730 THE list trim IS LOAD-BEARING. list prepend makes a LIST \, and g_oled's route matches a SELECTOR \, so without it every parameter is silently rejected and the display just shows zero., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 2 5 0;
#X connect 4 1 9 0;
#X connect 4 0 7 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 1;
#X connect 8 0 9 1;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 7 0 12 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 13 0 12 1;
#X connect 12 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X restore 20 540 pd controls;
#N canvas 30 30 1700 900 transport 0;
#X text 20 20 The six transport buttons \, on their own channel. PLAY and STOP drive the clock \, LOOP selects the mode \, and REW / FF / REC are visibly alive and visibly unassigned until something wants them., f 58;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 190 spigot;
#X obj 160 150 r \$0-xport-on;
#X obj 20 240 select 127;
#X obj 20 290 f;
#X obj 160 250 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 20 340 - 40;
#X obj 20 400 select 1 2 3 4 5 6;
#X msg 20 470 xport-rew 1;
#X obj 20 520 s disp;
#X obj 220 470 t b b;
#X msg 220 540 xport-play 1;
#X obj 220 590 s disp;
#X obj 380 540 bang;
#X obj 380 590 s start;
#X msg 540 470 xport-ff 1;
#X obj 540 520 s disp;
#N canvas 40 40 900 700 mode-toggle 0;
#X text 20 20 LOOP IS A TOGGLE THAT PD OWNS. The button is momentary and the mk1 has no LED \, so the only place the mode can live is here. f starts at 0 \, so the first press goes compose to perform., f 52;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 190 f 0;
#X obj 160 150 r \$0-mode-state;
#X obj 20 240 + 1;
#X obj 20 290 mod 2;
#X obj 20 340 t f f;
#X obj 200 400 s \$0-mode-state;
#X obj 20 400 select 0 1;
#X obj 20 460 t b b;
#X obj 320 460 t b b;
#X msg 20 520 compose;
#X msg 160 520 status compose;
#X msg 320 520 perform;
#X msg 480 520 status perform;
#X obj 20 580 s mode;
#X obj 160 580 s disp;
#X obj 320 580 s mode;
#X obj 480 580 s disp;
#X text 20 640 THE STATE COMES BACK BY SEND \, not by a cord. A cord from the trigger up to f's cold inlet would run straight through + 1 and mod 2 \, and a \$0- send inside an abstraction is exactly what the convention allows this for., f 46;
#X text 460 640 THE MODE GOES OUT TWICE \, deliberately: bare on the mode bus for u_err's filter \, and as status for the footer. It cannot be a disp PARAMETER \, because g_oled runs parameter values through makefilename %g \, which refuses a symbol., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 1 7 0;
#X connect 6 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 8 1 10 0;
#X connect 9 1 12 0;
#X connect 9 0 11 0;
#X connect 10 1 14 0;
#X connect 10 0 13 0;
#X connect 11 0 15 0;
#X connect 12 0 16 0;
#X connect 13 0 17 0;
#X connect 14 0 18 0;
#X restore 720 470 pd mode-toggle;
#X obj 920 470 t b b;
#X msg 920 540 xport-stop 1;
#X obj 920 590 s disp;
#X obj 1080 540 bang;
#X obj 1080 590 s stop;
#X msg 1240 470 xport-rec 1;
#X obj 1240 520 s disp;
#N canvas 40 40 900 600 unmapped-xport 0;
#X text 20 20 A seventh number on a channel that carries exactly six. It means the nano's scene was rebuilt \, or a factory reset wiped it -- REC + STOP + SCENE held at power-on does that \, which is worth knowing so you do not do it by accident., f 52;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 200 f;
#X obj 160 160 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 20 260 makefilename cc-%d-unmapped;
#X obj 20 310 list prepend warn m_nano;
#X obj 20 360 list trim;
#X obj 20 410 s err;
#X text 20 470 No flags to clear here \, unlike the control side: the transport path gates on the value alone \, so a rejected button simply emits nothing., f 52;
#X obj 20 170 t b;
#X text 300 200 THE t b IS THE BUG FIX. select's reject outlet emits the float it did NOT match -- cc minus 40 -- and a float on f's HOT inlet overwrites the stored CC instead of reading it \, so an unknown CC 47 reported itself as cc-7. Caught by tools/phase4-bench.pd \, not by reading., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X restore 1420 470 pd unmapped-xport;
#X text 20 680 PRESS ONLY \, then decode. select 127 comes before the CC is even read \, so a release cannot reach any of this -- and PLAY firing on release as well as press would double every transport command., f 46;
#X text 420 680 EACH BRANCH HAS ITS OWN s disp. Sends are not a shared object \, so five of them cost nothing and keep every branch a self-contained column -- which is what stops the cords crossing., f 46;
#X text 820 680 PLAY AND STOP ALSO HIT start AND stop \, allowlist buses that nothing consumes until Phase 5. Wiring them now means Phase 5 has a working transport the moment u_tempo exists., f 46;
#X text 1180 680 LOOP writes the mode to the FOOTER rather than showing it as a parameter \, and REW / FF / REC report only their own names. Visibly alive and visibly unassigned beats silently dead., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 6 0 5 1;
#X connect 5 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 8 1 11 0;
#X connect 11 1 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 11 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 8 2 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 8 3 18 0;
#X connect 8 4 19 0;
#X connect 19 1 20 0;
#X connect 20 0 21 0;
#X connect 19 0 22 0;
#X connect 22 0 23 0;
#X connect 8 5 24 0;
#X connect 24 0 25 0;
#X connect 8 6 26 0;
#X restore 340 540 pd transport;
#X obj 1180 400 loadbang;
#X obj 1180 440 del 2000;
#X obj 1180 480 f \$1;
#X obj 1180 520 print m_nano-control-channel;
#X text 1180 570 Says which block it is listening on \, once \, a couple of seconds in. THE DELAY IS NOT COSMETIC: deploy.sh gates on OUTPUT rather than exit status \, and quits the check immediately after load \, so a print at loadbang would fail every deploy. This way the diagnostic survives where it is needed -- the by-hand SSH console -- and the check stays silent., f 40;
#X text 20 780 WHAT IS NOT HERE: any notion of what a slider DOES. The names are generated -- slider-1 \, knob-3 \, btn-t-5 -- and that is deliberate \, because there are no parameters to name until v0.3. A lookup table pretending to be a mapping would be a lie \; generated names are honest about being placeholders., f 58;
#X text 480 940 Nothing here scales a value. Sliders and knobs report raw 0-127 and whatever consumes them decides what that means \, so the same surface can mean different things in compose and perform without this file changing., f 46;
#X text 860 780 ctlin's outlets are value \, controller \, channel \, and Pd fires RIGHT TO LEFT -- so channel lands \, then the controller \, then the value that triggers everything. VERIFIED off the wire rather than assumed: the very first event of a session already carries the right controller and channel \, which cannot happen unless both were stored first. This repo has been bitten here before \, by polytouchin emitting note before value., f 46;
#X connect 3 0 12 0;
#X connect 3 1 4 0;
#X connect 3 2 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 6 1 9 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 12 1 14 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 18 0;
